                <pb facs="0525" n="445" xml:id="pg445"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">832.00 Revolutions/148: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Consul at Bahia</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Briggs</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Bahia</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1930-10-25T09:00:00-03:00">October 25, 1930—9
                        a.m.</date><lb/>[Received October 25—7:08 a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>A little trouble last night in downtown district but in general quiet, and
                    Coronel Ataliba Osorio in temporary control. <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Pensacola</hi> arrived yesterday afternoon about 5 o’clock.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Briggs</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
